---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy - Harness Dreams";
const description =
  "Privacy policy for Harness Dreams, covering the local-first macOS tester app, local telemetry processing, share cards, and the waitlist website.";
const repoUrl = "https://github.com/reachjalil/harness-health";
---

<SiteLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="page-hero policy-hero">
      <div class="container page-hero-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</span>
          <h1>Harness Dreams is local-first by design.</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            This policy explains what the website and local macOS tester app
            collect, how local session telemetry is processed, how share cards
            work, and what choices you have.
          </p>
          <p class="policy-date">Effective date: July 3, 2026</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="policy-summary card" aria-label="Privacy summary">
          <span class="mono">Short version</span>
          <ul>
            <li>Raw transcripts, code, secrets, and Dream Score history stay on your Mac.</li>
            <li>Waitlist sign-up collects your email address and basic request metadata.</li>
            <li>The tester MVP has no cloud sync, mobile companion, payment, or account surface.</li>
            <li>Share cards are explicit exports from a preview, not automatic sharing.</li>
            <li>We do not sell personal information or share it for cross-context behavioral ads.</li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="section policy-body">
      <div class="container section-narrow">
        <h2>Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy applies to the Harness Dreams marketing site, the
          waitlist form, and the local macOS tester app. Some repository names,
          package names, or
          repositories, package scopes, or domains may still use historical
          project names while the product moves to Harness Dreams.
        </p>

        <h2>Information the website collects</h2>
        <p>
          If you join the waitlist, the site sends your email address, a hidden
          spam-prevention field, and a source label to the waitlist API. The
          site is served through Cloudflare, which may process standard request
          metadata such as IP address, user agent, timestamps, URLs requested,
          and security signals needed to operate, protect, and debug the site.
        </p>
        <p>
          In local development or if the backend is not configured, the waitlist
          form may store a note only in your browser's local storage. That local
          note is not sent to us unless you submit it to a configured endpoint.
        </p>

        <h2>Information the local app processes</h2>
        <p>
          Harness Dreams is built to track AI coding harness activity on your
          machine. Depending on what you enable, the local app may read or
          generate session transcripts, prompts, agent thinking blocks, tool
          calls, file paths, project metadata, model and token usage, Codex
          token estimates, Dream Scores, code-flow stages, trends, highlights,
          quotes, hidden quote choices, share-card previews, advice dismissals,
          and app settings.
        </p>
        <p>
          By default, that app data is processed and stored locally. Raw
          transcripts, source code, secrets, credentials, and private repo
          contents are not sent to Harness Dreams servers simply because you run
          the local app.
        </p>

        <h2>Optional local runner text</h2>
        <p>
          The MVP score, trends, highlights, and quote ranking are deterministic
          local computations. If you enable local runner features, a local
          Claude or Codex CLI may phrase quote captions or advice cards from
          already-selected evidence. That runner is for words only; it does not
          write scores, change formulas, or apply project changes.
        </p>

        <h2>Share cards</h2>
        <p>
          Share cards are created only when you choose to render one. A card can
          include a Dream Score, band, mini code-Code Flow graph, one stat, one quote,
          date, and Harness Dreams wordmark. Quotes are redacted again at display
          time. Exporting or sending the resulting PNG is your action, outside
          the app's control.
        </p>

        <h2>Features not in the tester MVP</h2>
        <p>
          The tester MVP does not include accounts, cloud sync, iPhone or Apple
          Watch companion apps, encrypted backup, payments, live sharing, or
          server-side leaderboards. Those parked features would require updated
          product surfaces and may require an updated policy before launch.
        </p>

        <h2>How information is used</h2>
        <p>We use information for these purposes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Operate the site, waitlist, and local tester app.</li>
          <li>Generate local Dream Scores, code-Code Flow graphs, trends, highlights, quotes, advice cards, and share-card previews.</li>
          <li>Respond to sign-ups, support requests, bug reports, and security issues.</li>
          <li>Protect the service from abuse, spam, fraud, and operational failures.</li>
          <li>Improve product reliability, privacy protections, and documentation.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How information is shared</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell personal information. We do not share personal
          information for cross-context behavioral advertising. We may share
          information with service providers that help operate the site,
          waitlist API, security, analytics if enabled, or support tooling.
          Those providers are allowed to process information only for the
          service purposes we authorize.
        </p>
        <p>
          We may disclose information if required by law, to protect rights and
          safety, to investigate abuse, or as part of a merger, acquisition, or
          similar transaction involving the project or service.
        </p>

        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>
          Local app data stays on your device until you delete it through the
          app, remove the application data, or change retention settings.
          Hidden quotes, dismissed advice cards, and share-card export history
          are local app data. Waitlist email addresses are kept until you ask to
          be removed or until the waitlist is no longer needed.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can choose not to join the waitlist, not to enable local runner
          captions/advice, not to export share cards, and not to include private
          projects in tracking. You can delete local app data from your machine.
          You can ask to
          access, correct, export, or delete personal information we control,
          subject to identity verification and applicable law.
        </p>
        <p>
          Privacy rights vary by location. California residents and residents of
          other jurisdictions may have rights to know, access, delete, correct,
          opt out of certain sharing, limit use of sensitive personal
          information, or appeal a decision. Harness Dreams does not knowingly
          sell or share personal information for behavioral advertising.
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          The product is designed around data minimization, local-first storage,
          secret redaction, explicit share-card previews, and advice-only cards.
          No security program can guarantee perfect protection, but the intended
          posture is to collect less, keep sensitive work local by default, and
          make cloud use explicit.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          Harness Dreams is intended for developers and is not directed to
          children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information
          from children under 13.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy as the product, parked sync/mobile/payment
          features, or legal requirements change. Material changes should be
          posted on this page with a new effective date.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Until a dedicated privacy email is published, contact the project
          through the public GitHub repository:
          <a href={repoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">
            {repoUrl}
          </a>.
          Do not include secrets, private transcripts, or sensitive code in a
          public issue.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .policy-hero {
    background:
      radial-gradient(70% 80% at 88% 8%, rgba(167, 218, 211, 0.2), transparent 56%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, var(--bg), var(--bg-soft));
  }

  .policy-date {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
  }

  .policy-summary {
    padding: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 1.8rem);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }

  .policy-summary ul,
  .policy-body ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .policy-summary li,
  .policy-body li {
    margin-block: 0.45rem;
  }

  .policy-body {
    padding-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .policy-body h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.4vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .policy-body h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .policy-body p {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }

  .policy-body a {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
</style>
